    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10181" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-foedĕro</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>, ātum, 1, <i>v. a., to unite</i> or <i>join by a
				league</i> (mostly in eccl. Lat.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sabinae impiis nuptiis confoederatae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Oros. 2, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: membra, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 2, 437: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amicitiam nascentem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 4</span></i>
			, n. 1 al.</div>
